swer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c90c1939-4375-5af7-bd4d-c8b99fda5bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567222} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ec2b10-de4d-5b62-bfc2-36a4e5c13d13" :answer-field/key "$H(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2)\\,i-{e}^{xy}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e2a1d7f-e53f-5a9c-a708-98dd5132af11" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $H(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y>2\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $G(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $H(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2)\\,i-{e}^{xy}\\,j$; $G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aab6b82-5473-54b2-8342-d5b12a067309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567189} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0e194e-4e46-543a-b453-b158f7199720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.ty